; Nested block tree used by the Phase 3 scanner / Scope-trip tests.
; One top-level cave block (doghill) with two levels of children, one
; empty block (sump), and a distinct station count per block so a test
; can tell them apart:
;   doghill                    3 stations (d1, d2, big-passage.p1)
;   doghill.big-passage        4 stations (p1, p2, p3, east.e1)
;   doghill.big-passage.east   5 stations (e1 .. e5)
;   doghill.big-passage.sump   0 stations
; *fix d1 plus the cross-scope shots keep the whole file one connected
; component, so cavern solves it.
; Dates are deliberately uneven so the Scope-trip seeding tests can tell
; the three cases apart: big-passage writes a range (its start date is
; what a trip takes), east writes none and inherits big-passage's,
; doghill writes none at all and keeps CaveWhere's default.
*begin doghill
*fix d1 0 0 0
*data normal from to tape compass clino
d1 d2 10.0 0 0
d2 big-passage.p1 2.0 0 0

*begin big-passage
*date 2024.01.05-2024.01.07
p1 p2 5.0 90 0
p2 p3 4.0 90 0
p3 east.e1 1.0 0 0

*begin east
e1 e2 3.0 45 0
e2 e3 3.0 45 0
e3 e4 3.0 45 0
e4 e5 3.0 45 0
*end east

*begin sump
*date 2025.03.15
*end sump
*end big-passage
*end doghill
